{
  "name": "nist_sp_800_171",
  "annotations": [
    {
      "tag": "cprt_framework_version",
      "value": "SP_800_171_3_0_0"
    },
    {
      "tag": "publication_date",
      "value": "2024-05"
    },
    {
      "tag": "oscal_content_tag",
      "value": "v1.6.0"
    },
    {
      "tag": "oscal_content_commit",
      "value": "f0de6d8d8c059d374f15e0ae07508d82e370fc1d"
    }
  ],
  "description": "A LinkML model of NIST Special Publication 800-171 Revision 3, the security requirements for protecting controlled unclassified information (CUI) in nonfederal systems and organizations: its seventeen requirement families, each security requirement with its statement, discussion, references and source controls, the organization-defined parameters (ODPs) a requirement leaves to the organization, and the assessment objectives and methods that SP 800-171A Revision 3 gives each requirement.",
  "title": "Protecting Controlled Unclassified Information in Nonfederal Systems and Organizations (SP 800-171 Revision 3)",
  "comments": [
    "The version is the revision of SP 800-171 the schema renders, written as NIST's Cybersecurity and Privacy Reference Tool numbers it (SP_800_171_3_0_0), and source is the publication's digital object identifier. The catalog NIST publishes for that revision in usnistgov/oscal-content, which carries the assessment procedures of SP 800-171A Revision 3 as well, is copied to src/nist_sp_800_171/schema/oscal-content/ at the tag and commit in the annotations. scripts/check_upstream_release.py reads the same pins and reports when NIST publishes a newer revision or changes the catalog. The catalog's own metadata version (1.1.0) numbers the catalog, not the publication. The release tags are the schema's own versions.",
    "SP 800-171 is a work of the United States Government and is not subject to copyright in the United States. The descriptions here are this project's own words; NIST's text of each requirement, discussion, parameter and assessment procedure stays in the catalog copy.",
    "NIST's catalog renders each family as an OSCAL group, each security requirement as an OSCAL control of class requirement, each statement item, discussion, assessment objective and assessment method as a part, each organization-defined parameter as a parameter, and each reference and source control as a link to a back-matter resource. The broad_mappings name those lmodel/oscal classes."
  ],
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-171r3",
  "see_also": [
    "https://lmodel.github.io/nist-sp-800-171",
    "https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/171/r3/final",
    "https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-171Ar3",
    "https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/protecting-controlled-unclassified-information",
    "https://github.com/usnistgov/oscal-content/tree/v1.6.0/nist.gov/SP800-171/rev3"
  ],
  "id": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-sp-800-171",
  "version": "3.0.0",
  "imports": [
    "linkml:types"
  ],
  "license": "Apache-2.0",
